Package: beidan
Title: Beijing Match and Parlay Research Pipeline
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Beijing Lot", "Contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "hh.earlydays@gmail.com")
Description: Explicit-input match probability projection and configurable
    parlay group construction, ticket valuation, constrained allocation,
    settlement and diagnostics with synthetic fixtures. One plan uses a single
    leg count (6, 7 or 8), with a session-scoped parlay settings block.
    Includes the shared Python cutoff-driven historical learning backend.
License: file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.3.0)
Imports: checkmate, S7, tibble, dplyr, tidyr, lubridate,
    reticulate, rlang, stats, utils, httr2 (>= 1.3.0)
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), callr, knitr, pkgload
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
